    "status": "present",
    "value": "Construct the lexicographically largest sequence with one1 and two copies of each2..n, separated by their own value. The approach is: descending choices at first empty position; first complete distance-valid sequence is lexicographically maximal. Its target cost is exponential bounded backtracking/O(n) auxiliary, n<=20. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
